{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787237159,"nonce":"CLqMKgqVd9McXEK3wQwFIAuOuHE=","message":"Done, on the owner's ruling: **an ephemeral listing the labels, not a modal.**\n\n**Why not a modal, recorded because the option's value implied one.** `views.open` needs a `trigger_id`\non §H.8's 3-second synchronous path — the same constraint that made `0a8ca4a` choose a `static_select`\nover a modal for the snooze presets — and it is a second interaction type `parseSlackEnvelope` refuses\nby design. The option had carried a `labels|\u003cid\u003e` value for a modal nobody ever built, so the press was\nanswered with silence, against §B.8.6's *\"Buttons are never no-ops.\"*\n\n**How the split works.** `oto.more`'s arm now branches on the **value**, not the id: `labelsSubject`\ncuts the one prefix both ends share and rejects a missing id, a nil uuid and a third field, exactly as\nits sibling `snoozeSubject` does. The four url options carry no value, so they stay inert unchanged and\n`oto.noop.*` keeps its own arm. The prefix is a shared constant (`domain.ShowLabelsValuePrefix`) minted\nby `overflowMenu`, and the bytes are still `labels|` — so **no golden moved and neither corpus was\nregenerated**. `overflowMenu`'s doc comment, which falsely claimed the action id was in the `oto.noop.*`\nfamily, is corrected.\n\n⭐ **No `WithUniquePeriod` on the job, deliberately.** For the writing verbs collapsing a replay is a\nconvenience over an idempotent write; here the outcome IS the reply, so a collapsed second press would\nbe an unanswered press.\n\n**Length is bounded and the truncation says so.** `labelListText` sorts by name, heads with\n`*All labels* (N)`, and reserves room for its worst-case suffix BEFORE the first line — the `1cd496f`\nlesson, where a truncator that never measured its own suffix could exceed the very limit it enforced.\nOverflow reads \"… 45 more labels not listed\" rather than stopping mid-list. Each name and value is\nrune-clipped so one 4 KiB value cannot cost the other labels their place, and values are escaped\nbecause they are upstream text.\n\n**Wiring.** The labels come through a new nil-tolerant `Labels` port. ⚠️ It shipped **unwired** and was\ncompleted separately: `app.slackLabelReads` resolves the Alert through the Case (the card names a Case;\nlabels live on the Alert) and is injected in `app.container` with a line in `app.assertions` — which\nthat file earns here, because a nil port degrades to an honest ephemeral instead of failing a build, so\nnothing else would notice the wiring being dropped. `lintreach` caught the agent's own\n`//oto:reachable-ok` suppression going stale the moment the adapter landed; it is deleted.\n\n**Docs.** SPEC §H.8's `oto.more` row now says what it does and marks the modal ⛔ with the reason;\n§H.8's 3-second paragraph records that **oto opens no modal at all today** and that a future one must\nbe argued against that paragraph. The runbook's known-gap note is replaced.\n\nGates: full `-race` suite, `golangci-lint` 0 issues, `lintreach` 0 new, vocabulary 60 (baseline),\nhelm/dto/server/generate/validators, `ui-build`, `ui-test`.","files":null}]}